.TH KAZ 1 2026-08-04 "kaz" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kaz \- pipe data to an honest terminal plot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kaz
.I chart
.RI [ FILE ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.I data
| \fBkaz\fR \fIchart\fR \fR[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kaz
plots data from standard input (or a file) to the terminal, one subcommand per
chart type. The plot is written to
.B stderr
by default, so
.B stdout
stays free for data; with
.B \-O
the input is echoed through, letting the plot sit in the middle of a pipeline.
Color auto\-detects from the destination stream. The automatic glyph tier uses
quadrants in UTF\-8 and ASCII otherwise; dense tiers are explicit. Where the terminal
speaks a pixel protocol the plot panel upgrades to a real image.
.PP
Input is parsed as whitespace\-separated fields, not CSV. For real CSV,
pre\-shape upstream with
.BR xsv (1)
or
.BR mlr (1).
.SH CHARTS
.TP
.B line \fR(\fBl\fR)
Line chart, one line per series.
.TP
.B scatter \fR(\fBs\fR)
Scatter plot.
.TP
.B bar \fR(\fBb\fR)
One bar per label (\fIlabel value\fR rows).
.TP
.B hist
Histogram; automatic bins, or \fB\-\-bins N\fR.
.TP
.B count \fR(\fBc\fR)
Value frequencies as bars.
.TP
.B density \fR(\fBd\fR)
Kernel density estimate.
.TP
.B ecdf
Empirical cumulative distribution.
.TP
.B box
A box plot per column (columns are groups).
.TP
.B violin
A violin plot per column.
.TP
.B hist2d
2D histogram (density grid) of \fIx y\fR points.
.TP
.B heatmap
Shade a row\-major matrix (first line on top).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " TARGET"
Plot destination: stderr (default), \fB\-\fR for stdout, or a FILE.
.TP
.B \-O
Pass input through to stdout (mid\-pipeline mode).
.TP
.BI \-d " CHAR"
Field separator (default: any run of whitespace).
.TP
.B \-H
First row is a header; its names label the series.
.TP
.BI \-\-fmt " FMT"
Column mapping: \fBy\fR, \fBxy\fR, \fBxyy\fR, \fBxyxy\fR, or \fByx\fR.
.TP
.BI \-w " N\fR, \fB\-h " N
Frame width and height in cells (0..4096, at most 4194304 cells; default: detected). Note:
.B \-h
is height; help is
.B \-\-help
only.
.TP
.BI \-t " TITLE"
Plot title.
.TP
.BI \-\-xlabel " TEXT\fR, \fB\-\-ylabel " TEXT
Axis titles.
.TP
.BI \-\-xlim " A,B\fR, \fB\-\-ylim " A,B
Fix an axis range.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-x ", " \-\-log\-y
Log\-scale an axis.
.TP
.B \-\-time\-x
Read the x column as time: unix epoch, or an ISO\-8601 subset.
.TP
.BI \-\-bins " N"
Histogram bin count (1..1000000; default: automatic).
.TP
.BI \-\-cols " LIST"
Select and reorder columns before any chart reads them: comma\-separated header
names (with \fB\-H\fR) or 0\-based indices.
.TP
.BI \-\-by " COL"
Scatter only: pull one column out as categories \(em each group gets a palette
color and a legend entry \(em and plot the remaining columns as x and y.
.TP
.B \-\-emit\-code
Print the equivalent malevich Rust program, with the parsed data inlined,
instead of the plot. A copy\-pasteable starting point for graduating a piped
chart into a program.
.TP
.BI \-\-colormap " MAP"
Heatmap/hist2d colors: \fBviridis\fR (default), \fBmagma\fR, \fBcividis\fR,
\fBgreys\fR, \fBred\-blue\fR, or \fBpurple\-orange\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-midpoint " V"
Center the colormap on value \fIV\fR, spanning the colorbar symmetrically \(em
the honest encoding for signed data (heatmap/hist2d).
.TP
.B \-\-log\-color
Logarithmic colormap: equal color steps per decade, for values spanning orders
of magnitude (attention weights, spectral power). Zeros and negatives render
as gaps. Mutually exclusive with \fB\-\-midpoint\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-labels\-x " A,B,..."
Band labels across the heatmap columns (comma\-separated). The count must
match the matrix.
.TP
.BI \-\-labels\-y " A,B,..."
Band labels down the heatmap rows, top to bottom. With labels the matrix reads
in input order, like the printed matrix.
.TP
.BI \-\-reduce " R"
How a heatmap denser than the terminal summarizes each screen bucket:
\fBmean\fR (default), \fBmax\fR, \fBmin\fR, or \fBmedian\fR.
\fBmax\fR keeps sparse spikes visible.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " WHEN"
\fBauto\fR (default), \fBalways\fR, or \fBnever\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-charset " SET"
\fBauto\fR (default), \fBascii\fR, \fBhalf\fR, \fBquad\fR, \fBsextant\fR,
\fBbraille\fR, or \fBoctant\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-pixels " WHEN"
\fBauto\fR (default), \fBalways\fR, or \fBnever\fR \(em sixel/kitty/iTerm2 image
panel.
.TP
.B \-q
Suppress the unparsed\-values tally.
.TP
.B \-\-live
Stream stdin, repainting a line in place (line only). See LIVE.
.TP
.BI \-\-window " N"
Live sliding\-window length (1..1000000; default: the frame's data width).
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " N"
Live repaint throttle (1..1000; default: 10).
.TP
.B \-\-rate
Live: plot the per\-sample delta of a monotonic counter.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show help; per chart,
.B kaz
.I chart
.BR \-\-help .
.SH LIVE
.B \-\-live
reads stdin forever, one value per line, and repaints a sliding window in place;
the final frame survives in scrollback, and Ctrl\-C restores the cursor. If a
live plot looks frozen, the producer is buffering \(em unbuffer it at the source
with
.BR "stdbuf \-oL" ,
.BR "grep \-\-line\-buffered" ,
or
.BR "awk '{print; fflush()}'" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MALEVICH_CHARSET
Overrides automatic glyph selection. Accepts \fBascii\fR, \fBhalf\fR, \fBquad\fR,
\fBsextant\fR, \fBoctant\fR, or \fBbraille\fR. Use a dense tier only when the
configured font supports it.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
A non\-empty value disables color.
.TP
.B CLICOLOR_FORCE
A non\-empty value other than 0 forces color even when the destination is not a tty.
.SH EXAMPLES
Plot a training curve:
.PP
.RS
.EX
cat loss.tsv | kaz line \-t training
.EE
.RE
.PP
Histogram a log field, count status codes:
.PP
.RS
.EX
awk '{print $5}' access.log | kaz hist
cut \-f2 species.tsv | kaz count
.EE
.RE
.PP
Sit mid\-pipeline; watch a live ping:
.PP
.RS
.EX
cat data.tsv | kaz line \-O | next\-tool
ping \-i.2 host | grep \-oE 'time=[0-9.]+' | tr \-d 'time=' | kaz line \-\-live
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR youplot (1),
.BR ttyplot (1),
.BR xsv (1),
.BR mlr (1).
.PP
Project: https://github.com/shergin/malevich
